WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:04.810
We're willing to bet most of you know Zoe
Saldana as the green-skinned, universe-saving,

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:07.500
Gamora from Guardians of the Galaxy.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:10.950
But you probably don't know about Saldana's
storied past.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:15.580
Long before she became a staple in the Marvel
Cinematic Universe, she was on a trajectory

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:17.869
toward superstardom.

00:00:17.869 --> 00:00:19.300
Dancing in the Dominican Republic

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:26.000
Born in 1978, Zoe Yadira Saldana Nazario was
hit with tragedy at a young age.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:31.119
Her father, Aridio Saldaña, died in a car
accident when Saldana was just nine years

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:32.119
old.

00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:36.450
After spending her childhood in Jackson Heights,
Saldana was uprooted and relocated to the

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:39.500
Dominican Republic following her father's
passing.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:43.920
With her mother and her sisters Cisely and
Mariel, Saldana settled into her new life

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.290
and discovered her love of dance, and especially
ballet.

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:50.490
After a while, however, Saldana's passion
for dance faded.

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:56.450
In the 2012 debut issue of Cosmopolitan for
Latinas magazine, Saldana dished on why she

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:58.520
ditched the dancing dream, saying,

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:03.180
"I had to quit ballet because it felt like
a part of me was dying inside.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:07.550
It takes a lot of courage to face up to things
you can't do because we feed ourselves so

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:09.530
much denial."

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:14.200
The relentless full-body immersion in ballet
took a physical toll as well, and she soon

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:18.020
realized she, quote, "didn't have the feet"
for ballet.

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:21.930
Saldana gave up the dream, but better things
were on the horizon.

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:23.260
Back to the Big Apple

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:28.720
In 1995, the Saldana family packed their bags
and returned home to New York, where Saldana

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:33.140
started working with the New York Youth Theater,
starring in a production of Joseph and the

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:35.110
Amazing Technicolor Dreamcoat.

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:39.659
Her performance landed her an agent who helped
snag her a guest role in everyone's favorite

00:01:39.659 --> 00:01:41.840
murder show, Law &amp; Order.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:46.690
Saldana popped up in two 1999 episodes, "Merger"
and "Refuge: Part 2".

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:52.000
Though she went uncredited for her first appearance,
her next gig made her someone to watch.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.060
Center Stage

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:57.860
Saldana broke through to the mainstream in
a big way: starring in the teen drama Center

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:01.690
Stage, a film, coincidentally enough, all
about ballet.

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:06.990
As the wickedly talented but sour-tongued
student Evanna "Eva" Rodríguez, Saldana showed

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:10.170
off her expert dance technique and stellar
acting chops.

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:15.220
Though it opened to mostly mediocre reviews,
Eva was the role that served as a launchpad

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:16.580
for Saldana's career.

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:21.220
Saldana herself has even noted that ballet
trained her for action, which she'd need for

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:22.900
what came next.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:24.470
Mega-stars

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:26.810
Saldana was up for increasingly prominent
roles.

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:32.640
In Britney Spears' 2002 coming-of-age road-trip
drama Crossroads, Saldana heard wedding bells

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:34.510
as the bride-to-be Kit.

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:39.060
Just 10 months later, she went back to her
dancing roots again to play Laila, the mysterious

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:42.030
love interest in the musical dramedy Drumline.

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:46.780
But Saldana wasn't just banking on a ballet
and beauty; she soon scored a lead in what

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:50.250
became one of Disney's biggest movie franchises
to date.

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:52.400
Pirates of the Caribbean

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:56.740
Saldana stepped into the swashbuckling Pirates
of the Caribbean: The Curse of the Black Pearl

00:02:56.740 --> 00:03:00.540
to play Anamaria, a victim of Jack Sparrow's
thieving ways.

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:05.040
Though the role saw her brush shoulders with
high-powered costars and offered her the chance

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:10.150
to work with acclaimed director Gore Verbinski,
it was one that nearly ruined her relationship

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:11.590
with acting forever.

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:15.989
During her time on set, she learned her worth
as a female in the business.

00:03:15.989 --> 00:03:20.530
Speaking with The Hollywood Reporter, Saldana
explained that unpleasantries behind the scenes

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:23.690
were enough to tempt her to quit acting for
good, saying,

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:25.550
"It was very elitist.

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:27.100
I almost quit the business.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:29.780
I was 23 years old, and I was like, 'F—
this!'

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:32.680
I am never putting myself in this situation
again.

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:36.690
People disrespecting me because they look
at my number on a call sheet and they think

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:37.980
I'm not important.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:39.940
F— you."

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:41.920
Star Trek stardom

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:46.450
Following a string of rom-coms like The Heart
Specialist and After Sex, Saldana boarded

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:49.080
the Enterprise in 2009 in J.J.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:51.080
Abrams' Star Trek reboot.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:55.801
Abrams himself asked Saldana to join the project,
and after he complimented her abilities, she

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:56.801
was sold.

00:03:56.801 --> 00:04:01.550
While not exactly a Trekkie herself, having
never seen the '60s show, Saldana portrayed

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:05.300
Star Trek fanatics in both The Terminal and
Guess Who.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:09.819
Saldana's mom, however, is a huge fan of Star
Trek and would often call Saldana on set to

00:04:09.819 --> 00:04:13.430
give her advice on how to approach the character,
telling MTV,

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:17.959
"She'd be like, 'Zoe, so for this scene when
you are in front of Spock, Uhura has to be

00:04:17.959 --> 00:04:22.650
stoic because she is elegant and remember
she's a translator so she is very sociable.

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:23.650
Okay?'

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:26.379
She would leave these messages and I was like,
'Who is this lady?'

00:04:26.379 --> 00:04:28.729
She's such a sci-fi geek!"

00:04:28.729 --> 00:04:34.240
Also in 2009, Saldana's role in the James
Cameron award-winning sci-fi epic Avatar raised

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:35.999
her profile to a new level.

00:04:35.999 --> 00:04:40.800
The film shattered Cameron's own 12-year record
for the highest-grossing film in history,

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:44.720
dethroning Titanic, but it wasn't a paycheck
gig for Saldana.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:46.439
She told The Hollywood Reporter,

00:04:46.439 --> 00:04:49.970
"You just gravitate naturally to what your
heart yearns for.

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:52.629
I grew up in a very science fiction-driven
household.

00:04:52.629 --> 00:04:57.100
It was odd for me to grow up and go out in
the world and not see other women going crazy

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:59.229
for science fiction."

00:04:59.229 --> 00:05:00.669
Going green

00:05:00.669 --> 00:05:06.289
Saldana's most recent scene-stealing role
is as Guardians of the Galaxy's badass galaxy-saving

00:05:06.289 --> 00:05:07.830
gal Gamora.

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:11.770
Director James Gunn approached her about playing
the green-skinned heroine, but her sister

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:15.020
had to get her up to speed on who the characters
even were.

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:16.889
Saldana admitted to MTV,

00:05:16.889 --> 00:05:22.539
"My sister sort of informed me of it, I read
the script and I was blown away with it."

00:05:22.539 --> 00:05:24.729
But she also had concerns about the role.

00:05:24.729 --> 00:05:29.789
During screen tests, Saldana stressed Gamora
stay "pretty" to draw teenage boys into seeing

00:05:29.789 --> 00:05:32.689
the film, Saldana explained in an interview
with Collider.

00:05:32.689 --> 00:05:37.259
"I don't know why I was stressing this a lot
but I really was when we were testing…

00:05:37.259 --> 00:05:38.870
I'm like, 'Pretty.

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:39.870
Teenage boys, please.

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:41.919
We gotta get their vote.'"

00:05:41.919 --> 00:05:44.870
In retrospect, her concerns seem fairly unfounded.

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:49.779
The superhero adventure nabbed the approval
of millions of adoring fans, not just adolescent

00:05:49.779 --> 00:05:50.779
guys.

00:05:50.779 --> 00:05:54.419
And being a part of the Guardians is something
Saldana truly cherishes, saying

00:05:54.419 --> 00:05:59.379
"We're kind of like the Rolling Stones of
the whole Marvel comics that I find so f—-ing

00:05:59.379 --> 00:06:00.379
appealing.

00:06:00.379 --> 00:06:04.479
We're like the ones who always fail in class
but for some reason we can burn the house

00:06:04.479 --> 00:06:05.960
down, and I like that."

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:07.639
Thanks for watching!

